        "title": "refactor(agents): trim embedded helper dead exports",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nThe production-mode Knip ratchet still listed 28 unused exports across the embedded-agent helper barrel, bootstrap defaults, and provider-error helpers. Several replay-history tests also depended on a dead barrel-only Google-model mock that production no longer reads.\n\nRelated: #105595\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\n- Remove redundant helper-barrel exports while preserving canonical owner modules.\n- Make implementation-only bootstrap and error helpers private.\n- Delete the fully orphaned HTTP-status classifier exposed by the visibility cleanup.\n- Point tests at canonical owners and exercise HTTP failover behavior through the public classifier.\n- Delete obsolete replay-history mock controls that only covered the dead barrel export.\n- Regenerate the global baseline on current `main`; concurrent mainline changes added 10 non-agent plugin entries, while this PR removes all 28 targeted `src/agents` entries.\n\n## User Impact\n\nNo user-visible behavior change. This narrows internal TypeScript module surfaces and reduces the enforced `src/agents` dead-export inventory from 537 to 509 entries relative to the branch base.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- `pnpm deadcode:exports:update` — stable exact-base baseline at 5,688 entries.\n- `pnpm deadcode:exports` — passed.\n- Focused embedded-helper suites — 441 tests passed.\n- Focused replay-history suites — 81 tests passed.\n- `pnpm check:changed` — passed on Blacksmith Testbox, including core/test types, formatting, lint, SDK baseline, and architecture guards.\n- Fresh autoreview — no accepted/actionable findings, confidence 0.98.\n\nNo changelog entry: internal dead-code and test cleanup only.\n",
